  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id)\n(section) R.C. 3509.04\n(quote) If the elector does not provide the elector's driver's license number or the last four digits of the elector's social security number on the statement of voter on the identification envelope, the elector also shall include in the return envelope with the identification envelope a copy of the elector's current valid photo identification, a copy of a military identification, or a copy of a current utility bill, bank statement, government check, paycheck, or other government document ... that shows the name and address of the elector.\n(section) R.C. 3509.05\n(quote) If the elector does not provide the elector's driver's license number or the last four digits of the elector's social security number on the statement of voter on the identification envelope, the elector also shall include in the return envelope with the identification envelope a copy of the elector's current valid photo identification, a copy of a military identification, or a copy of a current utility bill, bank statement, government check, paycheck, or other government document ... that shows the name and address of the elector.\n(section) R.C. 3509.07\n(quote) or that the elector has not included with the elector's ballot any identification required under section 3509.05 or 3511.09 of the Revised Code, the vote shall not be accepted or counted.\n(section) R.C. 3509.04 (voter statement form)\n(quote) (Voter must provide one of the following:) My driver's license number is ............... (Driver's license number). The last four digits of my Social Security Number are ............... (Last four digits of Social Security Number). ...... In lieu of providing a driver's license number or the last four digits of my Social Security Number, I am enclosing a copy of one of the following in the return envelope in which this identification envelope will be mailed: a current and valid photo identification, a military identification, or a current utility bill ...\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule)\n(section) R.C. 3503.15(H)(1)\n(quote) The secretary of state and the registrar of motor vehicles shall enter into an agreement to match information in the statewide voter registration database with motor vehicle records for the purpose of verifying the accuracy of the information in the statewide voter registration database and the information provided on voter registration applications, as required under 42 U.S.C. 15483.\n(section) R.C. 3503.15(H)(4)\n(quote) Notwithstanding any provision of the Revised Code to the contrary, a mismatch shall not be the sole reason for the removal of a voter from the statewide voter registration database.\n(section) R.C. 3503.15(H)(5)\n(quote) 'mismatch' means any of the following data fields that are not identical to one another with respect to a particular individual when information in the statewide voter registration database is compared to motor vehicle records: (a) Driver's license number; (b) Social security number; (c) Date of birth.\n(other) R.C. 3501.07: board of elections member appointment process revised\n(other) R.C. 3501.90: board / election-related provisions amended (election observer and litigation-related text)\n(other) R.C. 3503.15: statewide voter registration database; Secretary of State and BMV match records and tell boards of mismatches; boards tell voters and let them correct\n(other) R.C. 3505.21: election observers may serve at the board or another designated site while absent ballots are cast in person\n(other) R.C. 3509.01 / 3511.xx: period for casting absent ballots in person revised; same-day registration and absentee application generally barred\n(other) R.C. 3509.06: boards must notify absent voters when the identification envelope statement is incomplete (incomplete statement means ballot rejected)\n(other) R.C. 3509.07 / 3511.11: ballot not counted if the envelope statement is incomplete\n(other) version: 00_IN: carries absentee ID text (3509.04/05: DL number, last 4 SSN, or copy of photo ID / utility bill etc.); no in-person ID, no citizenship text\n(other) version: 01_RS: same absentee ID text; adds mismatch (DL/SSN/DOB) provisions in 3503.15 and observer text\n(other) version: 02_PS: same absentee ID text as 01_RS\n(other) version: 03_RH: same absentee ID text; no in-person ID or citizenship text\n(other) version: 04_PH: same absentee ID text\n(other) version: 05_EN: same absentee ID text; no in-person ID, no citizenship proof\n(other) note: 2008 PDF text: struck and new words are not marked, so I cannot tell which of the absentee ID wording was already law and which is new in this bill; the bill title says it makes the envelope statements required for a ballot to count. The absentee ID wording appears in every version. Vote-to-version mapping follows the brief (committee-reported version; concurrence on the version passed by the House); the as-passed Senate version is 02_PS. No in-person ID rule and no citizenship proof in any version. 'id_text_in_voted_version' is true for c (absentee ID) only.",
